# Citation metadata for the SOFTWARE ARTIFACT only.
#
# This file describes the simulation code and its frozen release. It
# deliberately contains NO paper DOI, no journal, no volume and no
# publication date, because the manuscript built on this artifact is
# unpublished. Inventing publication metadata for an unsubmitted paper
# would be a fabrication that survives in every downstream citation.
#
# When the manuscript is published, add a `preferred-citation` block with
# the real DOI and venue, and only then.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its frozen simulation results, please cite the
  software release below.

title: >-
  SwarmDroneMATLAB: a pre-registered simulation campaign for causal
  ACK-assisted, AoI-aware event-triggered UAV swarm communication

abstract: >-
  MATLAB simulation campaign for communication policies in multi-UAV
  formation control. Implements periodic, state-event, acausal
  oracle-AoI and causal ACK-assisted AoI-aware event-triggered
  communication over a network model with loss, delay, jitter and
  out-of-order delivery, against double-integrator and 6-DOF quadrotor
  followers. The release is frozen and includes the persisted results of a
  pre-registered validation over 50 holdout seeds and 3400 runs, common
  random number infrastructure, nine runtime protocol invariants, a
  nine-file test suite, and single-command reproduction and clean-clone
  verification. Seven pre-registered claims that were tested and rejected
  are preserved as part of the release.

type: software

authors:
  - name: "SwarmDroneMATLAB contributors"
    # Individual authors are withheld in this draft, consistent with the
    # anonymised manuscript. Replace with named authors and ORCIDs before
    # any public release.

